{"availability":"available","full":"justinethier/cyclone","name":"cyclone","description":":cyclone: A brand-new compiler that allows practical application development using R7RS Scheme. We provide modern features and a stable system capable of generating fast native binaries.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Scheme","stars":885,"forks":49,"created":"2015-02-22T03:08:21Z","updated":"2026-03-13T02:47:34Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"http://justinethier.github.io/cyclone/","topics":["c","compiler","cyclone-scheme","garbage-collector","r7rs","scheme"],"demo":"http://justinethier.github.io/cyclone/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:04:17.299Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T13:04:17.299Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T13:04:17.299Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T13:04:17.299Z","stars":885,"forks":49}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Cyclone Scheme is a brand-new compiler that allows real-world application development using the R7RS Scheme Language standard. We provide modern features and a stable system capable of generating fast native binaries.","Cheney on the MTA is used by Cyclone's runtime to implement full tail recursion, continuations, and generational garbage collection. In addition, the Cheney on the MTA concept has been extended to allow execution of multiple native threads. An on-the-fly garbage collector is used to manage the second-generation heap and perform major collections without \"stopping the world\"."],"features":["Support for the majority of the Scheme language as specified by the latest R7RS standard.","New features from R7RS including libraries, exceptions, and record types.","Built-in support for Unicode strings and characters.","Hygienic macros based on syntax-rules","Low-level explicit renaming macros"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/justinethier/cyclone/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"c94176b3d3549d94dad68e12591dccac7dcd248b63e7f4107ff2643e1b